{
  "id": "s02-l07",
  "unit": "s02-consonants",
  "title": "Consonants 7: ড় ঢ় য়",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**A dot changes everything.**\n\n- ড + dot = **ড়** (`r`): a flapped r. Curl the tongue back and flick it forward, like *tt* in American *butter*: বড় (`boro`, big).\n- ঢ + dot = **ঢ়** (`rh`): the same flap with a breath. Rare: গাঢ় (`garho`, deep, of a colour).\n- য + dot = **য়** (`y`): very common between vowels: মেয়ে (`meye`, girl), কোথায় (`kothay`, where).\n\nWhen you see a dot under a letter, check it twice: ড is `d`, ড় is `r`.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "l-rra",
      "bn": "ড়",
      "tr": "ro",
      "en": "flapped r: tongue curled back, flicked forward (like the tt in American 'butter')",
      "notes": "Name: doye shunno ro (ড-য়ে শূন্য র), 'ড with a dot'. Encoded as ড + nukta (U+09A1 U+09BC). Sounds close to র; in casual BD speech often merges with it."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-rrha",
      "bn": "ঢ়",
      "tr": "rho",
      "en": "flapped r with a puff of breath",
      "notes": "Name: dhoye shunno ro (ঢ-য়ে শূন্য র). Encoded ঢ + nukta (U+09A2 U+09BC). Rare; usually said like ড়."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-yya",
      "bn": "য়",
      "tr": "yo",
      "en": "y as in 'yes' (often a glide between vowels)",
      "notes": "Name: ontostho o (অন্তঃস্থ অ). Encoded য + nukta (U+09AF U+09BC). Very common: মেয়ে, কোথায়."
    },
    {
      "id": "garho",
      "bn": "গাঢ়",
      "tr": "garho",
      "en": "dark / deep (of colour)",
      "notes": "Uses ঢ়. গাঢ় লাল = deep red. Native check: pronunciation often closer to 'garo'."
    }
  ],
